description:
## Why

fx-ic2's Acceptance is a published, reproducible, measured paired report. A failed threshold is
reported as failed, and the language gate stays open (D0). Protocol §6-§8 list what the report must
contain. This bead splits the old single grading bead (split review
tide-fx-ic2-split/review-opus.md, finding 6). Parent: fx-ic2.

## Scope

Write the gate report under trials/e1-checked/ in `.worktrees/<this id>`, from:

- the measures bead's measures file and per-trial records;
- fx-ic2.7's grader-review file;
- the classification file;
- fx-ic2's readiness, batch and audit comments.

It states:

- each §8 threshold as met or not met, with F, P and I per arm;
- the §7.3 details: I is the mean over passing trials only; threshold 3 is not met if either arm
  has no passing trial; and the all-60 mean with failures counted as 20, as information;
- the information-only bootstrap intervals and how wide they are;
- every trial's §7.4 record, published;
- the classification of every first-check and final failure, with its evidence and toolchain
  defects flagged;
- the per-trial concurrency reviews with cited lines;
- the integrity-flag decisions;
- the structure checks met only by a comment;
- any §6 suite-test removal and its disputed result;
- the infrastructure reruns, second-fault failures and audit findings per arm;
- the §2 resemblance notes, read into the results;
- every input identity:
  - R and the order hash;
  - state.json's identity record;
  - the frozen tree SHA-256 and tasks.md's SHA-256;
  - the measures script's revision and the output hashes;
- the commands that reproduce the grading from the stored snapshots, and the measures from the
  stored records.

Store the first and final snapshots and the per-trial records durably, where those commands can
reach them: in the repository under trials/e1-checked/, or in an archive whose SHA-256 the report
records. Raw logs may stay outside with their hashes.

Run the reproduction commands to show they work:

- the measures in full;
- the grading on a seeded random sample of at least 10 trials covering both arms, from the gate
  worktree and under the gate conditions: an E1-exclusive slot through heavy.sh, the run
  procedure's preflight, the tmpfs TMPDIR and the pinned build jobs.

The report says a failure truthfully. Completing E1 does not make a failed gate pass. It never calls
gate trials 1-3 a "pilot" (§9).

## Acceptance

- The report and the stored snapshots and records land on main under GOVERNANCE.md's Merge Rule:
  - for the docs, a Codex pass, then an Opus review round;
  - for any new script, a Codex pass, then an Opus converge round that reports instead of fixing.
  Each finding is fixed or rebutted and re-checked by its finder.
- The report contains every item the Scope lists.
- The reproduced measures match the published ones exactly, and every sampled trial's regrade
  matches its stored grade.
- fx-ic2 then closes on its own Acceptance. The language gate stays open if a threshold failed.

